**/.dockerignore
**/.env
**/.git
**/.gitignore
# Mirrors the .gitignore secrets exclusion (see repo-root .gitignore): these files can hold real
# local/production secrets on a developer's machine. Without this, `docker compose build` run
# locally would bake them into the image via the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` build stage — .dockerignore
# is evaluated independently of .gitignore, so it has to be listed here too, not just there.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Production.json

# User-uploaded files are local runtime data (mirrors the .gitignore exclusion for the same paths —
# .dockerignore is evaluated independently of .gitignore, same reasoning as the secrets block above).
# Without this, `docker compose build`/`docker build` on a machine where the app has actually run
# would bake real users' photos/documents into the image via `COPY . .`, and the image would then
# start serving other people's files in prod. App_Data/legal is deliberately NOT excluded here — those
# are committed legal document sources that must ship in the image (see ServiceBooking.API.csproj).
ServiceBooking.API/wwwroot/uploads/**
ServiceBooking.API/App_Data/private-uploads/**

# Serilog's rolling file sink (runtime log output) — not data or config, shouldn't be in the image.
ServiceBooking.API/logs/**

# Test run artifacts (coverage/trx output) — never needed inside the runtime image.
**/TestResults

**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm
**/azds.yaml
**/bin
**/charts
**/docker-compose*
**/Dockerfile*
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/obj
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
